  "id": "Compound::DB00641 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Simvastatin, a HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor, is linked to Cyp2c19 through a shared pathway involving Lovastatin. The evidence suggests that Simvastatin influences Cyp2c19 via Lovastatin, which binds to the enzyme. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate a causal link between Simvastatin and Cyp2c19 through the intermediate of Lovastatin. The lowest common ancestor of Simvastatin and Lovastatin is the HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor, and both are associated with the Delta-Lactone compound. The varying scores in the paths reflect the strength of the evidence, with the highest score (0.5123) indicating a stronger relationship. The mechanism involves the inhibition of HMG-CoA reductase, which leads to the production of Delta-Lactone, a compound that may modulate Cyp2c19 activity. The evidence suggests a potential regulatory role of Simvastatin on Cyp2c19, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
